    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for mingw-expat.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Expat is a C library for parsing XML documents. The mingw-expat packages provide a port of the Expat library for MinGW. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* libexpat: denial of service via crafted XML input (CVE-2026-45186)\n\n* expat: Expat: Denial of Service via quadratic complexity in attribute processing (CVE-2026-66046)\n\n* expat: Expat: Denial of Service via XML external entity parsing (CVE-2026-76641)\n\n* expat: Expat: XML Injection via Malformed UTF-16 Input (CVE-2026-93990)\n\n* expat: expat: Information disclosure via heap buffer over-read in XML_ParseBuffer (CVE-2026-77214)\n\n* expat: expat: Denial of Service via delayed entity amplification detection (CVE-2026-115506)\n\n* expat: expat: Denial of Service via NULL pointer dereference in external entity parsing (CVE-2026-117610)\n\n* expat: expat: Denial of Service via integer overflow during XML attribute parsing (CVE-2026-118370)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
        "text": "This content is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). If you distribute this content, or a modified version of it, you must provide attribution to the original copyright holder(s) and provide a link to the original.",
        "title": "Terms of Use"
      }
